A 2025 arXiv research paper by Shaul Zemel. Introduction

Consider, inside the ring
\mathbb{Q}[\mathbf{x}_{n}]
of polynomials in
n
variables (over
\mathbb{Q}
), the part
\mathbb{Q}[\mathbf{x}_{n}]_{d}
that is homogeneous of degree
d
